div.div:
preprocessor (mod.rs)
struct Trims { first, second }
Trim 1's tight box, and trim 2's only if it moved by more than TRIM_RECHECK_TOLERANCE_PX (working coordinates). Trims::NONE

preprocessor::optimizer
struct LetterboxReport { kinds, proxy, texture, bars, keep }
What detect_letterbox found: each edge's kind, the product proxy and the texture outside it, the content rect once the bars are cut (bars), and the rect to keep once the interior also reads as textured (keep)

center_and_stretch::grazes
struct Blocked { top, bottom, left, right, patch }
Per edge, one flag per line of the original (rows for left and right, columns for top and bottom): true = the product grazes there. patch: Edges. Blocked::any()

center_and_stretch::grazes
struct Edges { top, bottom, left, right }
One flag per edge: true = its blocked lines get the patch fill, false = a plain colour or ramp

center_and_stretch::gradients
struct Square<'a> { plan, subject, original, mask, blocked }
What blend needs to know about one composed square

center_and_stretch::gradients
struct Layout { red, green, yellow, blue, cyan }
Where each zone's fade starts and ends, in canvas pixels; None = the zone is not painted

center_and_stretch::gradients
struct Target { a, b, from, to, along_x }
The colour a zone fades into: a at from, b at to, a straight ramp between

center_and_stretch::patch
struct Scene<'a> { mask, origin, orig, margin_px }
What the patch fill needs to know besides the canvas pixels

shot_classifier::route
struct Shot<'a> { class, mask, bgc }
One image's verdict, the mask it was read from, and the BGC the colour sampler found (None: none dominated)

shot_classifier::route
struct Decision { route, subject, plan, note }
One routing decision: the route, the subject's box, the square R1 would cut, and a log line when the route is not the plain reading

shot_classifier::plan
struct Pins { top, bottom, left, right }
The sides the subject runs off the frame at: the square may not move them

shot_classifier::plan
struct SquarePlan { side, x, y }
The output square in original-image pixels. new(subject, margin, pins), real_region(), overhang()

shot_classifier::plan
struct Overhang { top, bottom, left, right }
How far the square reaches past each border: what R1 has to invent
